From: Jetha Chan <jetha@splatterfacegames.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: venc: encode the requested frame size by default

venc_try_fmt_common() rounds width up to 128 and height up to 32; for the
raw OUTPUT format that is the buffer layout the firmware expects (luma
stride and scanlines, chroma plane offset). venc_s_fmt() also used the
rounded values as the frame size given to the firmware
(HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_FRAME_SIZE) and as the crop rectangle, so a client
that sets no crop gets the padding encoded: firmware log for a 1280x720
request on MSM8953:

  SET_PROPERTY: FRAME_SIZE: ebufferType=1, nWidth=1280, nHeight=736
  frameWidthCoded: 1280 frameHeightCoded: 736

and a 490x652 camera frame would be coded as 512x672.

Keep the rounded format for the buffer layout and make the requested
size, clamped and made even, the frame size and the default crop
rectangle. VIDIOC_S_SELECTION still sets any smaller crop.

Tested on MSM8953 (Lenovo ThinkSmart View) with v4l2-ctl: requests of
1280x720, 490x652, 980x1304 and 1304x980 give streams of exactly that
size; a decoded 490x652 frame matches its source.

Signed-off-by: Jetha Chan <jetha@splatterfacegames.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
index eff5e230b..77e08dad4 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -290,6 +290,19 @@ static int venc_s_fmt(struct file *file, void *fh, struct v4l2_format *f)
 	inst->width = format.fmt.pix_mp.width;
 	inst->height = format.fmt.pix_mp.height;
 
+	/*
+	 * The alignment applied by venc_try_fmt_common() describes the
+	 * buffer layout (stride and scanlines of the raw frame). Encode the
+	 * size the client asked for: it is the default crop rectangle, and
+	 * VIDIOC_S_SELECTION can still change it.
+	 */
+	inst->width = min_t(u32, inst->width,
+			    ALIGN(clamp(orig_pixmp.width, frame_width_min(inst),
+					frame_width_max(inst)), 2));
+	inst->height = min_t(u32, inst->height,
+			     ALIGN(clamp(orig_pixmp.height, frame_height_min(inst),
+					 frame_height_max(inst)), 2));
+
 	if (f->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_OUTPUT_MPLANE)
 		inst->fmt_out = fmt;
 	else if (f->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE) {
